8. Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is Titanic Survival Prediction?

It is a machine learning project that predicts whether a passenger survived the Titanic accident.

Q2. Which type of machine learning is used?

Supervised learning.

Q3. Is it classification or regression?

Classification because the output has two classes: 0 and 1.

Q4. What is a Decision Tree?

A Decision Tree is a machine learning algorithm that makes predictions using a tree-like structure of conditions.

Q5. What is the target variable?

Survived.

Q6. What does Pclass mean?

Passenger class: 1st, 2nd or 3rd class.

Q7. Why do we handle missing values?

Because missing data can affect model training and predictions.

Q8. Why do we use Label Encoding?

To convert categorical text values into numerical values.

Q9. What is overfitting?

When a model performs well on training data but poorly on unseen data.

Q10. Which features affect survival?

Gender, age, passenger class, fare and family information can influence predictions.

9. Conclusion
Thus, a machine learning model was successfully developed using the Titanic passenger dataset to predict passenger survival based on passenger information. The model's performance was evaluated using accuracy and a confusion matrix.